# CodeSentinel

**Real static analysis meets multi-LLM insight — code review that doesn't need an API key to catch a bug.**

Paste a snippet or point at a file — get deterministic AST-based findings plus an optional narrative review from OpenAI, Anthropic, or a fully local Ollama model.

[![Python](https://img.shields.io/badge/Python-3.10+-3776AB?logo=python&logoColor=white)](https://python.org)
[![FastAPI](https://img.shields.io/badge/FastAPI-009688?logo=fastapi&logoColor=white)](https://fastapi.tiangolo.com/)
[![OpenAI](https://img.shields.io/badge/OpenAI-412991?logo=openai&logoColor=white)](https://openai.com)
[![Anthropic](https://img.shields.io/badge/Anthropic-Claude-D97757?logo=anthropic&logoColor=white)](https://anthropic.com)
[![Ollama](https://img.shields.io/badge/Ollama-Local_LLM-000000?logo=ollama&logoColor=white)](https://ollama.com)

</div>

---

## Features

| Feature | Description |
|---|---|
| **Real Static Analysis** | AST-based Python checks (bare excepts, mutable defaults, `eval`/`exec`, unsafe deserialization, hardcoded secrets, complexity) that run with zero API keys |
| **Multi-LLM Support** | Pluggable provider interface for OpenAI, Anthropic, and local Ollama — auto-detects whichever is configured |
| **Config-Driven Rule Engine** | Disable rules, override severities, or add custom regex rules per project via `.codesentinel.yml` |
| **Generic Language Checks** | Regex-based secret/SQL-injection/debug-statement checks for JS, Go, Java, Ruby, and more |
| **Report Exporting** | Markdown, JSON, or standalone HTML reports |
| **Web Dashboard** | Submit code, view findings and LLM insight, browse SQLite-backed review history |
| **CI-Friendly** | `--fail-on <score>` exits non-zero when quality drops below a threshold |

---

## Architecture

```mermaid
flowchart LR
    A["Code Input\n(file / snippet / dashboard)"] --> B["CLI or FastAPI Backend"]
    B --> C["Rule Engine\n(.codesentinel.yml)"]

    B --> D["Static Analyzer\n(Python AST)"]
    B --> E["Generic Analyzer\n(regex, other languages)"]
    B --> F["LLM Provider\n(OpenAI / Anthropic / Ollama)"]

    D --> C
    E --> C
    F --> G["Review Orchestrator"]
    C --> G

    G --> H["Scored Review Result"]
    H --> I["CLI Report\n(Markdown / JSON / HTML)"]
    H --> J["Web Dashboard\n+ SQLite History"]
```

---

## Tech Stack

- **Framework**: [FastAPI](https://fastapi.tiangolo.com/) + [Uvicorn](https://www.uvicorn.org/)
- **Frontend**: HTML5, CSS3, Vanilla JS
- **Static Analysis**: Python `ast` module, regex-based generic checks
- **LLM Providers**: [OpenAI](https://openai.com), [Anthropic](https://anthropic.com), [Ollama](https://ollama.com) (local, no API key)
- **Config**: [PyYAML](https://pyyaml.org/) (`.codesentinel.yml` rule engine)
- **Storage**: SQLite (review history)
- **Packaging**: setuptools, `src/` layout

---

## Quick Start

### Prerequisites

- Python ≥ 3.10
- (Optional) An OpenAI or Anthropic API key, or a local [Ollama](https://ollama.com) install, for the LLM insight pass

### Installation

```bash
# Clone the repository
git clone https://github.com/YOUR_USERNAME/codesentinel.git
cd codesentinel

# Create virtual environment
python -m venv .venv
source .venv/bin/activate   # macOS/Linux
# .venv\Scripts\activate    # Windows

# Install the package (editable) + dev/test dependencies
pip install -e ".[dev]"
```

### Configuration

Copy `.env.example` to `.env` if you want hosted LLM insight (entirely optional — static analysis works with none of this set):

```env
OPENAI_API_KEY=
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
OLLAMA_HOST=http://localhost:11434
```

### Run

```bash
# CLI: review a file, static analysis only
codesentinel review --file path/to/code.py --no-llm

# Web dashboard
codesentinel serve --port 8000
```

The dashboard opens at **http://127.0.0.1:8000/**.

---

## Project Structure

```text
codesentinel/
├── pyproject.toml               # Package metadata & CLI entry point
├── .codesentinel.yml.example    # Sample rule-engine config
├── src/codesentinel/
│   ├── cli.py                   # `codesentinel review` / `codesentinel serve`
│   ├── analysis/                # AST-based Python checks + generic regex checks
│   ├── providers/                # LLMProvider interface + OpenAI/Anthropic/Ollama backends
│   ├── rules/                    # Config-driven rule engine
│   ├── review/                   # Models, orchestrator, report exporters
│   └── web/                      # FastAPI app, dashboard frontend, SQLite history
└── tests/                        # pytest suite
```

---

## Usage

1. Run `codesentinel serve --port 8000` and open `http://127.0.0.1:8000/` in your browser.
2. Paste a code snippet, choose a language and provider (or leave it on auto-detect).
3. Click **Run review**.
4. Static findings appear instantly; if a provider is configured, an LLM narrative insight follows.
5. Past reviews are listed under **History**, persisted locally in SQLite.

Or skip the dashboard entirely and use the CLI:

```bash
codesentinel review --file app.js --language javascript --format json --output report.json
codesentinel review --file code.py --no-llm --fail-on 70   # CI quality gate
```

---

## Environment Variables

| Variable | Required | Description |
|---|---|---|
| `OPENAI_API_KEY` | No | Enables the OpenAI provider for LLM insight |
| `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY` | No | Enables the Anthropic provider for LLM insight |
| `OLLAMA_HOST` | No | Ollama server URL (default: `http://localhost:11434`) |
| `OLLAMA_MODEL` | No | Ollama model name to use (default: `llama3.1`) |

At least one provider is optional — CodeSentinel runs fully offline with `--no-llm` / `use_llm: false`.

---

## Docker Deployment

```bash
# Build the image
docker build -t codesentinel .

# Run the container
docker run -p 8000:8000 --env-file .env codesentinel
```

---

## Custom Rules

Copy `.codesentinel.yml.example` to `.codesentinel.yml` at your project root to disable rules, override severities, or add project-specific regex rules. See the file for examples.

---

## Tests

```bash
pytest
```

